  "result": "Perfect! All 95 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Added VAT calculations to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineVAT(line)`** \u2014 Calculates VAT per line:\n   - VAT = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100\n   - Rounded using `roundCents()` to handle fractional cents\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals (before discount/VAT)\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `vat`: sum of all line VATs (computed per-line, then summed)\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**Updated `renderInvoiceText`** \u2014 Now displays invoice breakdown:\n```\nDRAFT\nCustomer Name\n2\u00d7 Product @ \u20ac100.00 = \u20ac200.00\nSubtotal: \u20ac200.00\nDiscount: \u20ac20.00\nVAT: \u20ac38.00\nTotal: \u20ac218.00\n```\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- VAT computed per line on amount after discount (not on subtotal)\n- Line VATs rounded individually, then summed (never rounded at invoice level)\n- All amounts clamped at 0 (can never go negative)\n- Render shows optional lines (only if > 0) for subtotal, discount, VAT\n\n**Added 9 comprehensive tests** covering VAT calculations with various scenarios, discount interactions, and rendering.\n\nAll 95 tests passing (including all prior tests adjusted for new VAT structure).",
